The excerpt is a field-treatment protocol from Korean emergency-medical guidelines. It gives step-by-step rules for two trauma situations:  
1) managing an avulsed (knocked-out) tooth—control bleeding, keep the root untouched, transport the tooth in milk/ saline, and warn against wasting time searching for the tooth in major trauma;  
2) splinting fractures—apply a splint to limit movement, ease pain, and prevent further bone displacement during transport.

The excerpt is a field-treatment manual for Korean EMTs. It gives step-by-step protocols for three trauma situations:  
1) managing an avulsed (knocked-out) tooth—control bleeding, keep the root untouched, transport the tooth in milk/saline;  
2) splinting fractures—indications, universal splinting rules, and detailed use of air, vacuum and traction splints;  
3) stabilizing the pelvis—indications for suspected pelvic fracture/instability, goal of limiting internal bleeding, and precautions.
